## Algorithm Behavior Analysis

### **Brute Force (Naive Approach)**
- ❌ Tries every possible number in every cell
- ❌ No validation until end
- ❌ Maximum redundant calculations
- ❌ Extremely slow even for medium puzzles

### **Brute Force Dichotomique (Divide & Conquer)**
- ⚠️ Splits puzzle into sub-problems (divide)
- ⚠️ Solves independently (conquer)
- ⚠️ Merges solutions
- ⚠️ Better than naive but still slow
- ⚠️ Extra memory for storing sub-solutions

### **Backtracking (Constraint Satisfaction)**
- ✅ Validates constraints immediately
- ✅ Prunes invalid branches early
- ✅ Minimal redundant calculations
- ✅ Deep recursion but efficient
- ✅ Industry standard for CSP problems

